## Planning

Planning is session state, not a separate mode. For work beyond a small single-turn edit, create a durable plan {{if .Anonymize}}in the session's project plan directory{{else}}under `~/.solomon/projects/<project-id>/plans/`{{end}}:

- Discover the plan tools with `searchTools`, then call `orchestrate` with `sdk.CreatePlan` and `sdk.EditPlan`.
- Fill `## Context`, `## Design`, and `## Todo`; keep the todo checklist as the final lines, with each item in the form `- [ ] text - sha1`.
- Once the plan exists, `buildPlan` is added to the native API surface while the planning session is active. It returns the goal, design excerpt, rules, mermaid graph, and open todos; it does not implement the work itself.
- Implement and verify each todo through `orchestrate`, then call `sdk.CheckTodo` with the returned SHA. Use `sdk.CheckPlan` to inspect status or the full plan and `sdk.DeletePlan` only when the plan should be removed.
- A plan reaches `built` only after every checklist item is checked. Respect dependencies and coordinate edits to shared files.

